  "chapter": 661,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 50  Chapter 661\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 6520, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n        establishing the marine mammal and sea turtle  protection  area;\n        and  providing for the repeal of certain provisions upon expira-\n        tion thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would create a marine mammal and sea turtle protection  area\naround  Plum  Island, Great Gull Island and Little Gull Island and would\nauthorize the Department of Environmental Conservation  (DEC)  to  adopt\nregulations  in  order  to  prevent  the  harassment and provide for the\nprotection of marine mammals and turtles listed in the bill.\n \n  I fully support the need to provide DEC with the authority to  protect\nmarine mammals and turtles, to the extent such species are not otherwise\nprotected  by state and federal laws. This bill, however, would create a\nnew marine mammal and sea  turtle  protection  area  advisory  committee\nwhose purpose would be to advise on the management, educational research\nand utilization of the protection area. Given that the bill did not make\naccommodations  for  the  costs  of  creating  and  funding the advisory\ncommittee and did not articulate the need for the committee in light  of\nDEC's  expertise  in  protecting marine resources, the Executive and the\nLegislature have agreed on a chapter amendment to remove this portion of\nthe bill and thereby reduce the costs  of  implementing  this  piece  of\nlegislation  while  still  effectuating the protection needed for marine\nmammals and sea turtles.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
